t(regex_findall_variables(content)) return set() 里面有个regex_findall_variables函数： def regex_findall_variables(raw_string: Text) -> List[Text]: try: match_start_position = raw_string.index("$", 0) except ValueError: return [] vars_list = [] while match_start_position < len(raw_string): # Notice: notation priority # $$ > $var # search $$ dollar_match = dolloar_regex_compile.match(raw_string, match_start_position) if dollar_match: match_start_position = dollar_match.end() continue # search variable like ${var} or $var var_match = variable_regex_compile.match(raw_string, match_start_position) if var_match: var_name = var_match.group(1) or var_match.group(2) vars_list.append(var_name) match_start_position = var_match.end() continue curr_position = match_start_position try: # find next $ location match_start_position = raw_string.index("$", curr_position + 1) except ValueError: # break while loop break return vars_list 在这个函数中看到了 $ 符号的身影，就是在这里解析的了。而整个解析过程那是相当的复杂，没有用现成的包，而是作者自己实现的。并且还有个长达548行的parser_test.py测试代码，要说清楚，估计得另外再写一篇专项文章了。

